      "rev_n_8_8f0d4b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_8f0d4b_1",
        "node_id": "n_8_8f0d4b",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (revised): Dynamic Programming Approach\n\nWe will use dynamic programming to keep track of the minimum cost required to achieve a specific beauty level up to each tree. We'll maintain a DP table where `dp[i][j]` represents the minimum cost to color the first `i` trees such that the beauty of the coloring is exactly `j`. This approach ensures that we efficiently explore all possible ways to color the trees while maintaining the desired beauty level.",
