        "thought_text": "Thought-3 (Revised): Dynamic Programming with State Compression\n\nWe will use dynamic programming with state compression to keep track of the current state of the coloring process. We'll maintain a DP table where `dp[mask][beauty]` represents the minimum cost to color the trees up to the point where the subset of trees represented by `mask` is colored, with the given `beauty`. Here, `mask` is an integer where the binary representation indicates whether each tree is colored (1) or not (0). This approach allows us to efficiently explore all possible colorings while ensuring that we meet the desired beauty condition.",
